{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqbnqckziq0","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"task minting via file drop: adapters write stub task json files to designated folders, daemon pulls, sync endpoint","summary":"DECISION (supersedes the create task route decision): no HTTP task-creation route and no public create_task MCP tool. Every adapter mimics the Claude pattern — write a task stub JSON file into a designated per-harness folder under the daemon data dir; the daemon PULLS via aggregation + fs.watch exactly as it does for Claude native files. New POST /sync endpoint triggers an immediate pull and returns adopted keys plus inline link suggestions (the wiring nudge, in-band). Documented versioned stub format { id, subject, description, status, blockedBy, created_by { harness, agent_id } }; atomic tmp+rename writes; tolerant parsing. Harness-prefixed namespaces (cursor/, codex/, opencode/, local/) never collide with Claude session-uuid keys. Rationale: file writes survive daemon downtime where HTTP calls lose the task; minting decouples from deployment timing; adapter hooks and plugins run outside the agent tool gate so no gate exemptions needed; Claude stops being a special case — pull-from-files becomes THE model. writeStatus generalizes per-folder via the Phase 1 adapter seam. Plan doc: docs/multi-harness-plan.md on feat/harness-adapters.","created_by":null,"valid_from":"2026-06-13T01:08:59.315Z","vec":[-0.1374354511499405,-0.04739492014050484,-0.030665673315525055,0.017723986878991127,0.02684120275080204,0.012035364285111427,-0.011593330651521683,0.08317459374666214,-0.03490544483065605,0.024505654349923134,0.03129687160253525,0.02667444571852684,-0.0017774036386981606,0.10350818932056427,0.018191253766417503,-0.005999135319143534,0.009167936630547047,-0.021973881870508194,0.03326474875211716,0.010300780646502972,0.03506683558225632,-0.024247044697403908,0.003042055293917656,0.020840736106038094,0.005255617201328278,-0.0199624914675951,-0.021448029205